{number: 138}
{title: Where Jesus Is,’Tis Heaven}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
Since Christ my soul from sinnet free,
This world has been a heav’n to me
And mid earth’s sorrows and its woe
Ti’s heav’n my Jesus here to know.
Oh, hallelujah, yes ‘tis heav’n,
‘Tis heav’n to know my sins for giv’n
On land or sea, what matters where?
Where jesus is, ‘tis heav’n there.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
Once heaven seemed a far-off place,
Till Jesus showed His smiling face.
Now it’s begun with-in my soul,
‘Twill last while endless ages roll,
Oh, hallelujah, yes ‘tis heav’n,
‘Tis heav’n to know my sins for giv’n
On land or sea, what matters where?
Where Jesus is, ‘tis heav’n there.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
What matters where on earth we dwell?
On mountain top or in the dell
In cottage or a mansion fair
Where Jesus is ‘tis heaven there,
Oh, hallelujah, yes ‘tis heav’n,
‘Tis heav’n to know my sins for giv’n
On land or sea, what matters where?
Where Jesus is, ‘tis heav’n there.
{end_of_verse}
